From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:42:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs(process): a fork syncs from upstream at each cut tag,
 not continuously

AGENTS.md Issue Law: in a fork (an `upstream` remote exists), fetch
upstream's tags and fast-forward the fork's main to the newest vX.Y.0 cut
tag it lacks - never to upstream/main, which changes constantly - then
branch issue work from that main. Upstream conflicts are merged into the
issue branch only; the fork's main moves at the next cut tag. The
canonical repo (no upstream) keeps 'Start from the latest main'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
